Article 5 The Standing Committee of the National People's Congress shall, before the session of the National People's Congress is held, carry out the following preparatory work:
(1) proposing a draft agenda for the session;
(2) proposing a draft list of the Presidium and the Secretary-General;
(3) deciding on the list of persons to attend the session without voting rights;
(4) other preparatory matters for the session.

Article 10 The first meeting of the Presidium shall elect a number of standing chairmen of the Presidium, and shall elect a number of members of the Presidium to serve respectively as executive chairmen for each plenary session of the congress, and shall decide the following matters:
(1) the choice of deputy secretaries-general;
(2) the schedule of the session;
(3) the deadline for deputies to submit proposals during the session;
(4) other matters that need to be decided by the first meeting of the Presidium.
